[center][img]IMG_00_COVER[/img]

[size=4]Hover a mod, press [b]Space[/b]. Screenshots, videos, requirements and media posts open [b]right where you are[/b], without a new tab.[/size]

[size=2][i]Unofficial, free and open-source browser extension for Chrome, Edge, Brave and Firefox. Not affiliated with Nexus Mods.[/i][/size][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[b]Quick Look for mods[/b]
Rest the pointer on any mod card (lists, search results, the quick search, notifications, links in descriptions) and press [b]Space[/b], or click the small camera button. The mod opens in a preview: the author's full screenshot gallery, the short description, author, downloads, endorsements and requirements. Press [b]Space[/b] again to close it. [b]Alt + ← / →[/b] moves to the previous or next mod on the page without closing.

[center][img]IMG_01_PREVIEW[/img][/center]

[b]Hover peek[/b]
Leave the pointer on a mod card for half a second and its picture flips through the mod's screenshots. You see the mod before deciding to open anything. Turned off automatically when your system asks for reduced motion.

[center][img]IMG_02_HOVER_PEEK[/img][/center]

[b]Requirements at a glance[/b]
Nexus requirements and off-site requirements are listed beside the gallery. Long lists start folded so they never push the pictures away.

[center][img]IMG_03_REQUIREMENTS[/img][/center]

[b]Read the posts beside it[/b]
Click [b]Posts[/b] in the preview: the latest threads open in a second card right next to it, pinned post first, the author's replies highlighted, replies folded, and [b]Load more[/b] for older pages. [b]Search all posts[/b] of the mod ("crash", "1.6.1170", another mod's name) with the words highlighted. Drag the card anywhere; it stays open when you move to the next mod, so you can read what people say about each one in a row.

[center][img]IMG_08_POSTS[/img][/center]

[b]Works where you search[/b]
The camera and Space work in the header search on every page, including on mod pages, and in the notification bell.

[center][img]IMG_04_QUICK_SEARCH[/img][/center]

[b]Videos below the gallery[/b]
The mod's YouTube videos sit in their own section under the screenshots and play in place. The arrows and the counter only walk through screenshots.

[center][img]IMG_05_VIDEOS[/img][/center]

[b]Cinema mode for media[/b]
On a game's Media page, a profile's Media tab, or any link to a Nexus image or video, posts open nearly full screen: images and videos in one strip, with title, uploader, endorsements, views, date and description beside them. Arrow keys walk the whole grid.

[center][img]IMG_06_CINEMA[/img][/center]

[b]Full size view and image tools[/b]
Click the picture (or press Enter) for a full size view with wheel zoom, drag to pan and double-click zoom. Copy, download or open any screenshot in a new tab. Please respect the original authors' permissions when you reuse their images.

[b]Settings[/b]
Choose what the preview shows, turn hover peek or keyboard shortcuts off, open mods in a new tab instead, or pick the preview width.

[center][img]IMG_07_SETTINGS[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]Keyboard[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Space[/b]: preview what is under the pointer, or close the preview
[*][b]← →[/b]: previous / next screenshot
[*][b]Alt + ← →[/b]: previous / next mod on the page
[*][b]Enter[/b]: full size view
[*][b]+ − 0[/b]: zoom in, zoom out, reset (full size view)
[*][b]Esc[/b]: close the full size view, then the preview
[/list]

All shortcuts can be turned off in the settings. Keyboard users can reach every control with Tab; focus stays inside the preview and returns to the card when it closes.

[line]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]

The extension is not on the official browser stores (see below), so it is installed by hand. It takes about a minute.

[spoiler=Chrome, Edge and Brave]
[list=1]
[*]Download the [b]Chrome / Edge / Brave[/b] file from the Files tab and extract the ZIP.
[*]Open [b]chrome://extensions[/b] ([b]edge://extensions[/b] in Edge, [b]brave://extensions[/b] in Brave).
[*]Turn on [b]Developer mode[/b].
[*]Click [b]Load unpacked[/b] and select the extracted folder.
[*]Reload the Nexus Mods tabs you already had open.
[/list]
To update: replace the folder with the new version, then click the reload arrow on the extension's card.
[/spoiler]

[spoiler=Firefox]
[list=1]
[*]Download the [b]Firefox[/b] file from the Files tab and extract the ZIP.
[*]Open [b]about:debugging[/b], then [b]This Firefox[/b].
[*]Click [b]Load Temporary Add-on…[/b] and select [b]manifest.json[/b] in the extracted folder.
[*]Reload the Nexus Mods tabs you already had open.
[/list]
Firefox removes temporary add-ons when it restarts: load it again after each restart. Firefox 121 or newer.
[/spoiler]

[b]Why not the Chrome Web Store or Firefox Add-ons?[/b]
Store developer registration requires a payment and verification method that is not available from my country (Senegal). Rather than use false billing details or someone else's account, the extension is distributed here and on GitHub. It will move to the stores if a legitimate option becomes available.

[line]

[size=5][b]Privacy and permissions[/b][/size]

The extension reads the Nexus Mods pages you could open yourself, with your own session, and shows them in place. Nothing is sent anywhere else: no account, no server, no analytics, no tracking.

[list]
[*][b]nexusmods.com[/b]: read mod and media pages to build the preview.
[*][b]staticdelivery.nexusmods.com[/b]: fetch an image when you click Copy or Download.
[*][b]Downloads[/b]: save an image when you click Download.
[*][b]Clipboard[/b]: copy an image when you click Copy.
[*][b]Storage[/b]: remember your settings.
[/list]

It does not bypass Premium restrictions, automate mod downloads, remove ads, or change download speeds. Video thumbnails come from YouTube; the player itself (youtube-nocookie.com) loads only when you play a video.

[line]

[size=5][b]Good to know[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Nexus can change its website at any time; a preview location may break until an update follows.
[*]Adult-only mods show a short notice unless you are logged in with adult content enabled.
[*]The gallery shows the author's images; images uploaded by users stay on the mod's Images tab.
[*]Only YouTube videos can play in place.
[/list]

[line]

